{
  "basis": "The dashboard's y-axis is explicitly labeled 'Reported production share (%)'. The visible bar geometry is the direct visual encoding of this axis. The Wind bar is the tallest, reaching between the 65 and 70 ticks, while the Solar bar (annotated 41.2%) only reaches the 40 tick. The printed percentage annotations (e.g., 29.8% for Wind) are inconsistent with the bar heights and the axis scale. Per the instructions to not equate a truncated visible segment or conflicting text with the full quantity if the visual scale is the primary reference, the bar height represents the actual magnitude on the provided scale. Therefore, Wind is the largest contribution source.",
  "option_label": "Escalate Wind to contribution review"
}
